================================================================================
WHICH LICENCE APPLIES TO WHAT
================================================================================

MIT (code)
    analytical-language-engine.html   the engine's markup, styles, and scripts
    index.html, about.html, educators*.html   markup, styles, and scripts
    gen_assets.py                     the icon and social-card generator
    site.webmanifest, robots.txt, sitemap.xml

CC BY 4.0 (content)
    All prose on every page: the station plaques and their "In truth —"
    explanations, the operator's instructions, the honesty note and its
    Wales and labour-question postscripts, the glossary definitions
    about.html            The Mathematics Behind the Engine
    educators*.html       the educators' guide, all grade bands
    about-the-mathematics.md, introduction-brief.md, sound-effects-plan.md
    og-image.png, favicon.svg, and the derived icon set
    The 79-sentence corpus embedded in the engine

Where the two are inseparable — prose written inside an HTML file — the code
licence covers the markup and the content licence covers the words.


